<LegalPage
  title="Complaint Policy · Alliance Mutual Escrow"
  description="How complaints are handled at Alliance Mutual Escrow, and how to contact the DFPI, the state regulator for independent escrow companies."
  kicker="When something goes wrong"
  heading="Complaint policy"
>
  <h2>Start with us</h2>
  <p>
    Tell the officer on your file first; most problems are fixed the same day. If you would rather
    speak to management, ask for the escrow manager at (714) 544-6525 or write to
    <a href="mailto:info@ameescrow.com" style="color:var(--amber)">info@ameescrow.com</a> with your escrow number and what happened.
  </p>
  <p>
    A person reviews every complaint. We respond, in writing when you ask for it, and we tell you
    what we found and what we are doing about it.
  </p>

  <h2>Your right to go to the regulator</h2>
  <p>
    Alliance Mutual Escrow is an independent escrow company licensed by the California Department of
    Financial Protection and Innovation (DFPI). You may file a complaint with the DFPI at any time,
    whether or not you contact us first. The DFPI accepts complaints online at
    <a href="https://dfpi.ca.gov" rel="noopener" style="color:var(--amber)">dfpi.ca.gov</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What we will never do</h2>
  <p>
    We will not release funds without signed instructions, and we will not retaliate against anyone
    for complaining, to us or to the regulator. Neutrality is the product; accountability is part of it.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
